% Regression guard for GitHub issue #56.  As in abc2svg, a microtone
% follows a single ^ or _: F sharp raised by 1/4 of a semitone is ^5/4F.
% ^^ or __ followed by a microtone used to lose its sharp or flat without
% a message, and =^ or =_ was read as ^ or _.  They are now errors that
% give the valid spelling, and the note is played as a plain note, with
% the key signature and the earlier accidentals of the bar, as abc2svg
% plays it: ^^/4F is F sharp in G major, and F raised by 1/2 semitone
% after ^/F.
X:1
T:Double sharp or flat with a microtone
C:abc2midi test
M:2/4
L:1/4
K:G
^^/4F F|^/F ^^/4F|__/2B B|^^1G G|

X:2
T:Natural with a sharp or a flat
C:abc2midi test
M:2/4
L:1/4
K:F
=^/A A|=_B B|
